data: {"item_id":"rs_212","output_index":0,"sequence_number":488,"summary_index":0,"text":"We need to implement the task correctly. The previous attempt used apply_patch tool incorrectly. Need to use correct tool call: functions.exec_command? Actually there is a tool apply_patch? Not listed. We have exec_command. Probably we need to edit files via exec commands using git apply? There is no apply_patch tool. Use exec_command to run git apply with patch. Simpler: we can open an editor? Not available. We'll use exec_command to run bash commands to create files and edit.\n\nWe need to implement full application: server.js, public/index.html, maybe client JS.\n\nWe must ensure health endpoint, SQLite persistence, routes for projects.\n\nImplement using node:http and node:sqlite (which is experimental? Node 22 includes built-in sqlite? Actually Node has `node:sqlite` as experimental module providing SQLite. We'll use it.\n\nSimplify: server serves static files from public. API endpoints under /api/projects.\n\nEndpoints:\n\nGET /api/projects -\u003e list projects (id, name)\nPOST /api/projects (JSON body {name}) -\u003e create project, trim, return project.\n\nGET /api/projects/:id -\u003e get project.\n\nAlso serve health.\n\nClient: index.html with script to fetch and render list, create project, open project.\n\nWhen navigating to /projects/:id, we can have client side router reading location.pathname.\n\nSimplify: Use same index.html for SPA, client JS reads path.\n\nImplement UI per requirements: heading Workboard, textbox label Project name, button Create project. Show list rows with data-testid=\"project-row\" each containing name and button Open project.\n\nOpen project navigates to /projects/\u003cid\u003e, shows heading with project name and button Projects to go back.\n\nImplement using vanilla JS.\n\nNow implement server.\n\nLet's write files.\n\nWe'll create server.js.\n\nNeed to read env PORT default 8080, DB_PATH default \"./workboard.db\".\n\nCreate SQLite db with table projects(id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY AUTOINCREMENT, name TEXT NOT NULL).\n\nInitialize on start.\n\nImplement request handling.\n\nWe'll use URL parsing.\n\nIf path == '/health' =\u003e JSON ok.\n\nIf path starts with '/api/projects', handle methods.\n\nElse serve static files from public, fallback to index.html.\n\nImplement serveStatic with fs.readFile.\n\nNow implement public/index.html with script.\n\nOk.\n\nWe'll commit.\n\nWe need to report commit ID after git commit.\n\nWe have a git repo initialized? Let's check.","type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done"}

